# Why It Works — ignore generated caches and junk
# Keep the repo to source + deliverables. Generated/derived files are regenerable.

# HyperFrames thumbnail caches (auto-generated; mirror the asset tree and create
# very long nested paths that break Windows' path limit — never commit these).
.thumbnails/

# Node / tooling
node_modules/
.cache/
*.log

# Temp / scratch decode artifacts
*.raw
*.tmp

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.gstack/

# Full-length final video renders: too large for plain git (e.g. a 4K combine is ~240 MB)
# and GitHub LFS budget is exhausted. They live on YouTube + locally; keep them out of git.
# The small vertical shorts under output/shorts/ stay tracked. (2026-07-01)
projects/*/output/**/*.mp4
